# N5 -- numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py N5 (run from the repository root cft_cmi/).
# Discretisation: the lattice model itself, computed exactly in Gaussian form (every one-particle mode of
# every block kept; no truncation, no taper, flint ball arithmetic at bits_for(n)+200); the lattice
# spacing is the only regulator, and its effect is the resolution dependence measured below (no
# regulator-free discretisation exists for a lattice model; continuum statements are compared after
# extrapolation in n).  Raw data (one line per run, with the normalisation defect nrm):
#   numerics/networks/vwz_A.raw     <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py sweep e015
#   numerics/networks/vwz_B.raw     <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py sweep e005,e010
#   numerics/networks/vwz_C.raw     <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py sweep e020,e030,e040,m010,m020,m030
#   numerics/networks/vwz_G.raw     <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py sweep m020x,e030x,m010x,m030x
#   numerics/networks/chains_D.raw  <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py chains sw,eq3,eq4,eq5,eq6,n4r2
#   numerics/networks/chains_E.raw  <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py chains ref
#   numerics/networks/chains_F.raw  <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py chains n5r2,n4r3,n6r2,n5r3
#   numerics/networks/chains_H.raw  <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py chains eq3x,n4r2x
#   numerics/networks/chains_I.raw  <- $PYTHON numerics/networks/lattice_chain.py chains n6r2x
# Fit rules: NFIT = 4 finest resolutions, TOL_FIT = 1e-04 (fixed before the runs); see NETWORK_RESULTS.md.
# N5: where (H) fails (thm:general).  (a) Ex. 5.6 (lengths (1,1,1) m, start A_2, A_3 on A_2, then A_1 on
# A_2): Thm 5.2 swallows the first corner, prediction Phi_tot = Phi(second step alone) = 2 Phi_A(2/3).
# (b) REF-P6-0 geometry (13,21,9,17) m = (1.3,2.1,0.9,1.7): U = start A_2A_3, A_4 on A_3, A_1 on the
# UNION A_2A_3 (two corners: displaced mass at x_0 and p_4); Ud = A_1 on the WHOLE block A_2A_3A_4
# (degenerate step = global Moebius map: ONE displaced corner, an exact single-corner prediction);
# 3LR = control with A_B = A_2 (both corners at p_3, masses add).  Predictions: general rule (Thm
# 5.2, corner_measure) vs the naive (H) rule (mass sigma_1 at p_3), each through the single-corner law
# 2 Phi_A(zeta) per corner; for U the two-corner cross term (W2, Ghat unknown) is NOT included.

(a) Ex. 5.6: n=12 SW-S2=0.0e+00, n=18 SW-S2=0.0e+00, n=24 SW-S2=0.0e+00, n=36 SW-S2=0.0e+00, n=48 SW-S2=0.0e+00, n=72 SW-S2=0.0e+00
